      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We describe a case of spondylotic lumbar spinal stenosis in an infirm elderly patient successfully treated with multilevel laminotomies. This procedure is less stressful to patients than a full laminectomy. In a selected subgroup of patients with \"hourglass\" spondylotic stenosis, it may provide adequate decompression."},
